{"items":[{"tags":["c","file","file-io","relative-path","absolute-path"],"question_score":22,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":74990817,"is_answered":false,"question_id":11034002,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1672734880,"creation_date":1672734880,"body":"you can try to do something like this:\n\nif parent path does not exist (or fails for whatever reason), it will attach current directory in it&#39;s place.\n","excerpt":"from_str(&quot;somewhere/something.json&quot;).unwrap();\nlet parent = pbuf.parent().unwrap().canonicalize().unwrap_or(std::env::current_dir().unwrap());\nlet file = pbuf.file_name().unwrap().to_str().unwrap();\nlet <span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> &hellip; ","title":"How to get absolute path of file or directory, that does *not* exist?"},{"tags":["excel","vba","search"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":74985905,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1672697410,"creation_date":1672684378,"body":"Using 2010 Excel VBA - I need to use look up the image/pdf with the Branch Code as a part of its name at &quot;C:\\ECB Test\\ECB IR COPY&quot; and paste it at &quot;C:\\ECB Test\\&quot; RO if it exists. If it doesn&#39;t, the program needs to highlight the Branch Code.\n(File Name Examples: 28-Kochi-ecb-sdwan completed.pdf, 23 eCB Kozhikode completed.pdf/0036.jpeg)\nHaving done this manually twice for two other excel sheets (4k+ cells), I decided to Frankenstein a module together and, well, it does not work and I have no idea why.\n\n\nI think its unable to use the Branch Code variable as a wildcard, though I might as well have done something silly somewhere in the code. Can someone please help me out?\n","excerpt":"ECB Test&quot;\n    \n    Dim Row_Number As Integer\n    Dim fso As Object\n    Set fso = VBA.CreateObject(&quot;Scripting.FileSystemObject&quot;)\n    Dim Folder_Name As String\n    Dim Branch_Code As String\n    Dim <span class=\"highlight\">Final_Path</span> &hellip; 2)\n            Folder_Name = Worksheets(&quot;WAN RFP&quot;).Cells(Row_Number, 5)\n            \n            On Error Resume Next\n    \n            File = Dir(SRC_PATH &amp; &quot;\\*&quot; &amp; Branch_Code &amp; &quot;*&quot;)\n            <span class=\"highlight\">Final_Path</span> &hellip; ","title":"Unable to copy files (.pdf/.jpeg/.jpg) from one folder to another"},{"tags":["python","csv","sendgrid"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":74515774,"is_answered":false,"question_id":60011210,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1669017595,"creation_date":1669017595,"body":"Use following two functions:\n\nCall function read_csv_email(csv_path)\n","excerpt":"Use following two functions:\n def read_csv_for_email(<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>=None):\n    &quot;&quot;&quot; send_csv_email\n    Send final generated CSV file\n    :return:\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;\n    <span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> = &quot;sample/path/to.csv&quot;\n    df = pd.read_csv &hellip; (<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>, dtype=str, na_filter=True, index_col=False)\n    res = send_email_with_csv(\n        subject=&quot;Sending CSV with SendGrid is Fun&quot;,\n        content=&quot;&lt;strong&gt;CSV with Python&lt;/strong&gt;&quot;,\n        dataframe &hellip; ","title":"Sending email with Sendgrid using data from a csv"},{"tags":["python","dictionary","operating-system","pathlib","tomlkit"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":74427500,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1668885619,"creation_date":1668405888,"body":"I have a toml file that looks like\n\nI am turning this into a dict that looks like,\n\nThey key is  and the value is a dictionary. I want to check if  exists and for the dict in the value -- I want to check that the conf_path, prefix, suffix keys exist and that they all have a value that isn&#39;t  or .\nThis is what I have so far. I am having trouble checking the keys and values in default&#39;s value dict.\n\nHow can I check that the three specific keys exist and they each have a value?\nI don&#39;t know how to check that all three keys exist, they all have a value that isn&#39;t  or , and then say true if all of that is met.\nI can do one no prob though\n\nI was thinking use a list some how.\n","excerpt":"I am having trouble checking the keys and values in default&#39;s value dict.\ndef get_config_path() -&gt; str:\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;\n    default_path = os.path.expanduser(const.CONFIG_PATH)\n    <span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> = os.environ.get &hellip; (&#39;CONFIG_PATH&#39;, default_path)\n    return <span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>\n\n\ndef check_toml():\n    conf = Path(get_config_path())\n    default_table = [&#39;default&#39;, &#39;conf_path&#39;, &#39;prefix&#39;, &#39;suffix&#39;]\n    if conf.exists(): &hellip; ","title":"How can I check is each keys in this dict exist and that they all have a non empty value?"},{"tags":["python","if-statement","pathlib","tomlkit"],"question_score":2,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":0,"is_answered":false,"question_id":74455368,"item_type":"question","score":2,"last_activity_date":1668578106,"creation_date":1668574606,"body":"I have these two functions. The first one gets a file path ensures the file exists.\nThe second function is intended to check that a table exists in a toml file and then ensure three values exist and are not  or \nI am wondering how I can make it completely fail if any the table  or any of the three values don&#39;t exist.\n\nBasically, I want the second function to fail and tell either default is missing or one of the three values are missing - otherwise return .\nThe toml file looks like\n\nEdit;\nI think my best bet may be to raise a keyerror. But still thinking on best how.\n","excerpt":"are not None or &#39;&#39;\nI am wondering how I can make it completely fail if any the table default or any of the three values don&#39;t exist.\ndef get_source_path(env_var: str, default_path: str) -&gt; str:\n    <span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> &hellip; = Path(os.getenv(env_var, default_path)).expanduser().resolve()\n    if not final_path.is_file():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f&#39;File {<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>} does not exist&#39;)\n    return <span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>\n    \n\ndef check_toml &hellip; ","title":"Python - how to entirely stop a function if criteria is not met?"},{"tags":["python","pathlib","getenv"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":74429253,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1668418320,"creation_date":1668417172,"body":"I have the following code.  IS \n\nWhenever this uses , I&#39;d like it to use Pathlib&#39;s .\nIs the best way going to be to do something like\n\nIs there a way to use pathlib all together to be able to do either ~/ when it is that and then a direct path like /home/roland when it is like that?\n","excerpt":"():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f&#39;File {<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>} does not exist&#39;)\n    return <span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>\n\nWhenever this uses CONFIG_PATH, I&#39;d like it to use Pathlib&#39;s Path().resolve(). &hellip; Is the best way going to be to do something like\nif <span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> not &#39;~/winnie/poohbear.toml&#39; then Path(<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>).resolve()\nIs there a way to use pathlib all together to be able to do either ~/ when it &hellip; ","title":"Python - How to use os.getenv with Path().resolve()"},{"tags":["python","pathlib","getenv"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":74429489,"is_answered":false,"question_id":74429253,"item_ty